# Code owners: the changes RFC-0062 §12.3 reserves for a maintainer's approval, on top of the
# review agent's. Every rule names the maintainers in governance/maintainers.toml, and no rule
# ever names an agent identity (ADR-0021, RFC-0062 §12.6).
#
# There are no area owners. Everything not listed here merges on the gates and the review agent,
# including kernels, the solver and the rest of `net` and `cluster`.
#
# `cargo xtask ci lint` checks this file: every owner is a maintainer and none is an agent, every
# RFC-0062 §12.3 path class is covered, and no path outside them gets an owner. The check accepts
# `/dir/`, `/path`, `*` inside a segment, and bare names; see xtask/src/codeowners.rs.
#
# Three items on §12.3's list are not paths: a waived gate and a change no gate covers are
# enforced by labels (QUAL-E1-T18), and a new crate dependency by the dep-diff check
# (QUAL-E1-T19).

# CI and release configuration
/.github/                       @devdaviddr @xunholy
/ci/                            @devdaviddr @xunholy
/release-please-config.json     @devdaviddr @xunholy
/.release-please-manifest.json  @devdaviddr @xunholy
/version.txt                    @devdaviddr @xunholy
/deny.toml                      @devdaviddr @xunholy
/supply-chain/                  @devdaviddr @xunholy
/governance/                    @devdaviddr @xunholy

# Security-critical: the hardware dispatcher and lab configuration
/bench/lab/                     @devdaviddr @xunholy
/lab/                           @devdaviddr @xunholy

# Security-critical code, owned by module name until the tasks that write it place it. Key
# handling, signing and the update client, in any crate:
/crates/*/src/keys.rs           @devdaviddr @xunholy
/crates/*/src/keys/             @devdaviddr @xunholy
/crates/*/src/signing.rs        @devdaviddr @xunholy
/crates/*/src/signing/          @devdaviddr @xunholy
/crates/*/src/updater.rs        @devdaviddr @xunholy
/crates/*/src/updater/          @devdaviddr @xunholy
# Cluster admission and the cluster key, in `net` and `cluster`:
/crates/net/src/admission.rs    @devdaviddr @xunholy
/crates/net/src/admission/      @devdaviddr @xunholy
/crates/net/src/cluster_key.rs  @devdaviddr @xunholy
/crates/net/src/cluster_key/    @devdaviddr @xunholy
/crates/cluster/src/admission.rs    @devdaviddr @xunholy
/crates/cluster/src/admission/      @devdaviddr @xunholy
/crates/cluster/src/cluster_key.rs  @devdaviddr @xunholy
/crates/cluster/src/cluster_key/    @devdaviddr @xunholy

# Registering a new model family: the graph registry (RFC-0043 §1), not the family modules.
/crates/graph/src/families.rs       @devdaviddr @xunholy
/crates/graph/src/families/mod.rs   @devdaviddr @xunholy

# Agent instruction and configuration files: every entry of ci/agent-instructions.toml, which the
